// The dictionary: every thing the game has, every thing it means to have, and
// where each one's picture comes from. Read by com.kagebi.data.CodexCatalog and
// checked by CodexValidator at boot; see notes/d.md, "The dictionary".
//
// TWO KINDS OF ENTRY.
//   Live - names a def: "item": "potion_small". Its name, words and picture are
//     the def's own, so the dictionary cannot disagree with the game. EVERY gear,
//     stone, weapon, item, relic, crop and worker's good must be here exactly
//     once; the game refuses to start otherwise, and says which.
//   Planned - names no def. It is a picture the game means to use, written down
//     so the use can be chosen later: "status": "consider" for one still being
//     weighed. Named either by an "id" (and codex.item.<id> in the translations)
//     or by a "kind" and its number among that kind: the third unnamed sword is
//     sword_3, "Kiếm 3".
//
// PICTURES. "raven" lists cells of the Raven Fantasy Icons sheet, 1-based; cell N
// is the file Separated Files/16x16/faN.png (32x32: fbN, 64x64: fcN), at row
// (N-1)/16 and column (N-1)%16 of the sheet. Cells listed together are one
// thing at its successive levels, level 1 first, and how many there are is the
// grade: 6 levels S, 5 A, 4 B, 3 C, 2 D, 1 F. "variants": true is instead one
// shape in several colours: grade F, one level. "art" is a region of ui.atlas.
// "source" is the file in the pack, where the region's name cannot spell it.
//
// EQUIPMENT comes from the sheet's equipment block, rows 115 to 136, counted
// from 0 at the row of two witch hats: "row 1" below is sheet row 116. Rows 15
// to 18 of the block are not used, and the validator keeps them out.
//
// MAIN WEAPONS are the 80 steel shapes of sheet rows 90-94 (cells 1441-1520).
// Each is ONE weapon at three levels - steel, then gold (80 cells on), then blue
// (160 on), the strongest - so every weapon is grade C. All 80 must be listed,
// but for the five whose weapons left the game (CodexCatalog.RETIRED_SHAPES).
